<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Neurons Within LLMs</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LLMs are composed of multiple layers and every layer include two core blocks, i.e., attention and MLP blocks and there are two fully connection layer in MLP every MLP block. Existing studies find there are many neurons in MLP blocks. Formally <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao and Huang, 2025</a>)</cite>, let <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> de note the MLP block in the <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer, the forward process of the layer can be formulated as:</p>
<table id="A3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{l+1}=F(X_{l}W_{l1})W_{l2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{l+1}=F(X_{l}W_{l1})W_{l2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{l+1}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{l+1}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the output features of the MLP block, and <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the input features of the MLP block. <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{l1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{l1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times w}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{l2}\in\mathbb{R}^{w\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{l2}\in\mathbb{R}^{w\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the weight matrices of the two fully connection layers within the MLP block, respectively. Note that the bias parameters of fully connection layers are ignored for the simplicity. <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> represents the non-linear activation function.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In which, <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{l2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{l2}</annotation></semantics></math> can be reviewed as the set of neurons <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{l2}^{i},i=1,2,...,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{l2}^{i},i=1,2,...,d\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}=F(X_{l}W_{l1}),A\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}=F(X_{l}W_{l1}),A\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times w}</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly is the activation strengths of the neurons <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{l}^{i},i=1,2,...,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{l}^{i},i=1,2,...,d\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
